---

= Dough

Whisk @all-purpose flour{175%grams} with @granulated sugar{1%tbsp} and @salt{3%grams}.

Cut @unsalted butter{140%grams} into small pieces and fork it into the dry mixture until well incorporated, should be crumbly with small pieces of butter throughout.

> The original recipe uses a food processor, I don't have one but works well enough.

Once crumbly (and no dry flour), add @cold water{85%grams} and fold in with a spatula and form a ball.

> The original recipe has half this, this made it much easier to work with, but the crust stuck to the pan more than the 1/2 water versions, so I'll try again sometime to dial in this amount.

Wrap tightly in plastic and chill in the refrigerator for at least ~{2%hours}.

= Line Pie Pan

Grease the pie pan.

Roll out the dough to about 1/8 inch thick and 14 inches in diameter (big enough to fill the pie pan with an inch or more off the sides).

> Use flour on your rolling surface and pin as needed

Transfer to the pie pan and form it to its surface with your hands, cut excess dough from the sides leaving about an inch hanging over.

Fold the over-hang back into itself to thicken the edge of the crust (so it forms a thickened ring along the rim of the pie pan).

Chill in the refrigerator for ~{20%minutes}.

= Blind-bake the Crust

Prepare the dough and chill as directed.

Line the pie pan (see above).

Preheat the oven to 350°F.

Once chilled, line pie dough (in the pan) with aluminum foil and add weights (pie weights, beans, rice, sugar, etc.).

Bake for ~{1%hour}.

Remove from oven, remove weights, and let cool.